    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's just another way of saying \"make up your own distractions.\" it feels so artificial. like, if the end result is always going to be nothingness, why bother creating these tiny, temporary little anchors? it feels less like finding purpose and more like just trying to delay the inevitable. it's exhausting to keep pretending these small things matter when you know they don't.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
